&lt;h2&gt;About the Role&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;isSelectedEnd&quot;&gt;As a Senior Solution Architect at VTEX, you will be responsible for designing and delivering scalable commerce solutions for enterprise clients across both B2C and B2B business models.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;isSelectedEnd&quot;&gt;You will work closely with clients throughout the project lifecycle, from understanding business challenges and defining the solution architecture to supporting implementation, delivery, and ongoing evolution.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role combines strong technical expertise, business understanding, project ownership, and client relationship management. You will help clients translate complex business needs into clear, actionable, and scalable solutions, while ensuring projects are delivered on time, within scope, and with the expected business impact.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Your responsibilities will include:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Designing simple, scalable, and reliable solutions based on each client’s business needs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translating business requirements into clear architectures and implementation plans.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Supporting clients and partners throughout implementation and project delivery.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Helping ensure projects are delivered on time, within scope and budget, and with the expected business outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identifying technical risks, dependencies, and trade-offs, and recommending practical solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Facilitating discovery, business planning, and digital strategy workshops.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Building trusted relationships and acting as a technical and strategic advisor to clients.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working with Sales, Customer Success, Product, and systems integrators to deliver successful projects.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Communicating complex technical topics clearly to both technical and non-technical audiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contributing to architectural standards, knowledge sharing, and the continuous improvement of the Solution Architecture team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;For this position, you are required to attend the Barcelona office four days a week, from Monday to Thursday, with remote work on Fridays.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;About the Team&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;isSelectedEnd&quot;&gt;The Solution Architecture team helps enterprise clients design, implement, and scale their commerce operations with VTEX.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We connect business strategy, technical architecture, and project delivery, working closely with clients, implementation partners, and teams across VTEX. As a global team, we share knowledge across regions and continuously improve how we deliver complex B2C and B2B commerce projects.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Who you are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have experience designing and delivering complex digital, commerce, or enterprise technology solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You understand software architecture, APIs, integrations, data flows, and distributed systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have experience working on implementation or delivery projects with multiple teams and stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You can connect business objectives with technical decisions and translate complexity into clear actions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are comfortable working directly with enterprise clients and building relationships with technical and business stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You communicate clearly, facilitate effective workshops, and adapt your message to different audiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You take ownership, identify risks proactively, and manage multiple priorities effectively.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are collaborative, practical, curious, and motivated by solving complex business and technology challenges.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Previous experience with VTEX is desirable.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;hr&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;About VTEX&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div&gt;VTEX (NYSE: VTEX) is the composable and complete commerce platform that delivers more efficiency and less maintenance to organizations seeking to make smarter IT investments and modernize their tech stack. Through our pragmatic composability approach, we empower brands, distributors, and retailers with unparalleled flexibility and comprehensive solutions, enabling them to invest solely in what provides a clear business advantage and boosts profitability. VTEX is trusted by 2.400 global B2C and B2B customers, including Carrefour, Colgate, Motorola, Sony, Stanley Black &amp;amp; Decker, and Whirlpool, having 3.400 active online stores across 43 countries (as of FY ended on December 31, 2024).&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Founded in the year 2000, VTEX has a history of being unstoppable. Completely against the odds, VTEX is leading a high-tech industry and positioned above market giants. We are building an extraordinary future with more than 1,300 employees scattered across 25 locations in 16 countries in Latin America, North America, Europe, and Asia. For more information, visit &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.vtex.com&quot;&gt;www.vtex.com&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;At VTEX, you will work in a challenge-driven environment and collaborate with amazing peers. If you are powerful individually, join us, and we will be unstoppable together.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Benefits&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll be entitled to a comprehensive benefits package, including:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Meal voucher: €11 per day (based on 22 working days per month) via Pluxee&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Health insurance with Sanitas&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Life insurance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Friday in Focus: dedicated Friday afternoons for personal development and well-being&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Transportation Allowance (optional)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Workout benefit&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;+ many more!&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 14pt;&quot;&gt;ABOUT THE ROLE&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a Senior Software Engineer (L4) to join VTEX’s DOM team, working on one of the most strategic initiatives in the platform: the evolution of our Order Management and Order Allocation systems.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this role, you will help design and build a new agent-based order workflow, enabling merchants to customize how orders are processed, routed, and fulfilled across different use cases and markets.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a hands-on role where you will work on high-scale, mission-critical systems, solving complex problems at the intersection of distributed systems, platform architecture, and AI-driven orchestration.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 14pt;&quot;&gt;ABOUT THE TEAM&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
